 Whether it brings a revolution or not, but one thing is for sure, for the time being, people won't be able to trust hardware wallet manufacturers, and many will probably stop using them for the short run. Some will start renewing their wallets and seed phrases and apply passphrases which should have been done at the beginning, but others might stop using hardware wallets completely for the time being. Honestly, this is too heartbreaking to see. People have lost all their money that they have saved working for so many years, imagine working for 12 to 15 years, making money, and then investing that money in an asset, and then getting your wallet compromised, especially when you have always been told to use a hardware wallet because they are the safest.
 So many people would rather use a centralized exchange such as Binance to keep their assets than using a hardware wallet for now, because at least Binance says that the funds of their users are SAFU with them and if anything happens, they will be responsible unless individual accounts are compromised from user's ends and not because of the exchange or its security.
 This is the only revolution this attack is going to bring in this industry, and it's not a good one.
